adaptivedemux2: do not permanently pause all output on a transient FLUSHING

A single FLUSHING push freezes video AND audio here, silently. The output loop
serves every track from one task, so any non-OK push (flow-combined) hits
`goto pause` and stops that one task for good, and FLUSHING posts nothing at
all: only GST_FLOW_NOT_LINKED and <= GST_FLOW_EOS do. Field freezes on DASH
with a subtitle track show exactly that shape, output_time pinned AT the
watermark with the downloads parked, element still PLAYING, position stopped,
indistinguishable from a network stall. Nothing recovers it: of the three
gst_task_start sites, two re-pause instantly on the flow combiner's stored
FLUSHING and only a flushing seek resets it.

Recover instead, when the element is not itself flushing: clear that pad in
the flow combiner (gst_flow_combiner_update_pad_flow with GST_FLOW_OK, which
also refreshes last_ret, or the very next push of ANY pad recombines the
stored FLUSHING and re-pauses), mark the track discont, and keep draining the
track. Discarding rather than skipping is load-bearing: the track's
next_position has to keep advancing or global_output_position pins at its
minimum, the input wakeup never fires, and the freeze survives the patch.
Real flushing (priv->flushing, re-checked after the warning drops the lock)
and the NOT_LINKED/EOS/ERROR paths stay byte-identical.

This restores A/V only. When the FLUSHING came from a downstream multiqueue,
that single-queue is independently latched and clears only on a FLUSH_STOP at
its sink pad, so the affected track stays dead until a flushing seek. D3 and
D4 are one bug in two elements.

--- a/subprojects/gst-plugins-good/ext/adaptivedemux2/gstadaptivedemux.c
+++ b/subprojects/gst-plugins-good/ext/adaptivedemux2/gstadaptivedemux.c
@@ -190,6 +190,10 @@
   /* Pending track (which will replace track) */
   GstAdaptiveDemuxTrack *pending_track;
 
+  /* TRUE once a transient FLUSHING push was reported for this slot, so the
+   * warning is posted once per slot instead of once per racing buffer. */
+  gboolean warned_transient_flushing;
+
   /* TRUE if a buffer or a gap event was pushed through this slot. */
   gboolean pushed_timed_data;
 } OutputSlot;
@@ -3681,6 +3685,33 @@
       TRACKS_LOCK (demux);
       gst_adaptive_demux_track_update_next_position (track);
 
+      /* FLUSHING while this element is not itself flushing is transient:
+       * something downstream flushed and that buffer was doomed either way.
+       * Pausing here stops output for EVERY track for good with nothing
+       * posted. Clear the pad in the flow combiner (which stores FLUSHING and
+       * short-circuits on it) and keep draining this track: its next_position
+       * must advance or global_output_position pins here and the input wakeup
+       * below never fires. Any other pad's real failure still pauses. */
+      if (ret == GST_FLOW_FLUSHING && !demux->priv->flushing) {
+        slot->flow_ret = GST_FLOW_OK;
+        ret = gst_flow_combiner_update_pad_flow (demux->priv->flowcombiner,
+            slot->pad, GST_FLOW_OK);
+        track->output_discont = TRUE;
+        if (!slot->warned_transient_flushing) {
+          slot->warned_transient_flushing = TRUE;
+          TRACKS_UNLOCK (demux);
+          GST_ELEMENT_WARNING (demux, STREAM, FAILED, (NULL),
+              ("Discarding data on %s: downstream returned FLUSHING while this "
+                  "element is not flushing", GST_PAD_NAME (slot->pad)));
+          TRACKS_LOCK (demux);
+          /* A real flush can have started while the lock was dropped. */
+          if (demux->priv->flushing) {
+            ret = GST_FLOW_FLUSHING;
+            goto pause;
+          }
+        }
+      }
+
       if (ret != GST_FLOW_OK)
         goto pause;
     }
